    "narrative": "Today\u2019s outlook for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who carries our highest efficiency score of 74.56. He benefits from a favorable matchup against Yesavage, where the combination of park factors and a dynamic platoon advantage propels him into elite territory. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** remains a cornerstone of today\u2019s effort; assuming he hits atop the order as projected against Patrick Sandoval, his 73.48 score reflects the significant value of his projected batting position and park-adjusted ceiling. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a daunting task against the elite arm of Skubal\u2014resulting in a suppressed score of 46.70\u2014his presence in the three-hole forces his inclusion despite the steep penalty for facing a sub-3.00 xERA pitcher.\n\nThe deepest bench decision centered on **Wade Meckler**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a score of 46.14. While **Wade Meckler** offered intrigue as a bench option, he was squeezed out by the high-floor utility play of **Jackson Merrill**, whose 59.31 score was bolstered by a significant platoon advantage against Gabriel Hughes. We are also keeping a close eye on the secondary tier of our outfielders, where **Andy Pages** earns a solid 58.95 score; his speed remains a critical asset in our pursuit of stolen bases, and he is projected to benefit from a slow delivery out of the opposition's rotation.\n\nRisks for the slate are primarily meteorological. We are monitoring a 45% rain risk impacting **Drake Baldwin**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, which could shorten their outings or force mid-game substitutions. Furthermore, the lineup uncertainty surrounding **Cole Carrigg**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Andy Pages** introduces a layer of variance to their projected impacts. Should any of these players be dropped from their respective lineups, we are prepared to pivot to the high-upside utility of **Coby Mayo** or the peripheral value of **Luis Lara** to maintain our efficiency targets.",
